//! WPAD / KPAD controller layer (`0x801DE9D0`-`0x801E8DD0`).
//!
//! **What lives here.** The Wii Remote driver (`WPAD`) and the higher-level
//! pad layer (`KPAD`): per-channel control-block reset and bring-up, locked
//! field accessors, the Bluetooth connection/reset callbacks, accelerometer
//! deltas, the global sampling-mode setter, and the public sampling/connect
//! callback setters. Each channel owns a 0x9C0-byte control block published
//! through the pointer table at `0x8039E330`. The second pass adds the WPAD
//! start gate, the connection/setup helpers, and the KPAD status/callback
//! extension accessors.
//!
//! **Cluster map.**
//! - `0x801DF570` - per-channel control-block reset
//!   ([`wpad_control_init_801df570`]).
//! - `0x801DF7F0` - driver bring-up for all four channels plus the periodic
//!   sampling alarm ([`wpad_init_801df7f0`]).
//! - `0x801DFA50`-`0x801DFBD0` - WPAD start gate and connection setup
//!   ([`wpad_start_801dfa50`], [`fn_801dfbd0`]).
//! - `0x801DFB40`-`0x801DFD10` - locked field readers and the connection/reset
//!   callbacks ([`fn_801dfb40`], [`fn_801dfb90`], [`fn_801dfc40`],
//!   [`fn_801dfd10`]).
//! - `0x801E0CE0`-`0x801E0F40` - HID/status helpers and the per-channel link
//!   getter ([`fn_801e0ce0`], [`fn_801e0e40`], [`fn_801e0f40`]).
//! - `0x801E0D30`-`0x801E1060` - accelerometer deltas, mode setter and the two
//!   callback setters ([`fn_801e0d30`], [`fn_801e0f00`],
//!   [`kpad_set_sampling_callback_801e0fd0`],
//!   [`kpad_set_connect_callback_801e1060`]).
//! - `0x801E10F0`-`0x801E15F0` - KPAD callback slots and extension flags
//!   ([`fn_801e10f0`], [`fn_801e1150`], [`fn_801e1260`],
//!   [`fn_801e14e0`], [`fn_801e15b0`], [`fn_801e15f0`]).
//! - `0x801E0700`-`0x801E1DD0` - device-to-channel assignment, report-ring
//!   producers and the double-buffered report copy
//!   ([`fn_801e0700`], [`fn_801e11a0`], [`fn_801e12c0`], [`fn_801e1630`],
//!   [`fn_801e1820`], [`fn_801e18d0`], [`fn_801e19c0`], [`fn_801e1b70`],
//!   [`fn_801e1c90`], [`fn_801e1dd0`]).
//! - `0x801DE9D0`-`0x801E0820` - report sampling gate and the Bluetooth
//!   connect/disconnect handler ([`fn_801de9d0`], [`fn_801dfe00`],
//!   [`fn_801e0820`]).
//! - `0x801E3420`-`0x801E3920` - KPAD sampling-mode, readiness and channel
//!   state accessors ([`fn_801e3420`], [`fn_801e3460`], [`fn_801e34b0`],
//!   [`fn_801e35f0`], [`fn_801e3890`], [`fn_801e38d0`], [`fn_801e3920`]).
//! - `0x801E4A40`-`0x801E6A30` - command queue, extension handshake, detach
