/// otherwise through that node's predecessor) and boosts that node's count
/// by the remainder. Otherwise the node is appended at the tail: the tail
/// node keeps the previous holdback, and the list's pending total becomes
/// the node's full count. Either way the node's in-list flag (`+0x16`)
/// becomes `1`.
