/// Reports a completed PIN-code lookup to the BTM search callback.
///
/// Copies the stored PIN address and the three PIN bytes into the reply
/// payload, then either zeroes the name (when the reply record is null or its
/// first halfword is non-zero) or copies at most `0x20` name bytes and
/// terminates them. The result is delivered as event `2`.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_801fc104` at `0x801FC104` (192 bytes)
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/main-gb/export/801fc104_FUN_801fc104.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `reply` - name reply: 16-bit status at `+0`, 16-bit length at `+2` and the
///   name at `+4`; may be null.
///
/// # Returns
/// `()`.
///
/// # Side effects
/// One callback call through [`BTA_DM_SEARCH_CALLBACK`].
///
/// # Safety
/// A callback must be installed, and `reply` must be readable for
/// `4 + length` bytes when it is used.
///
/// # Confidence
