/// * `addr` - peer `BD_ADDR` word.
/// * `code` - three PIN-code bytes.
/// * `name` - NUL-terminated device name (only its first byte is tested).
///
/// # Returns
/// `0x0B` without a search callback, `1` otherwise.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Stores the pending PIN request, may start a BTM name request, and performs
/// one callback call.
///
/// # Safety
/// `code` must be readable for three bytes, `name` must be readable as a
/// NUL-terminated string, and the search callback must be installed for the
/// reply path.
///
/// # Confidence
